\vspace{2mm}
Finally, we mention that our choice of the Heisenberg Hamiltonian is motivated by a numerical exploration over various possible couplings. 
%
We found that the isotropic chain in a magnetic field leads to most appreciable violations in the optimized case when compared with other choices (Ising, or XX or XXZ Hamiltonians).
This might be due to the isotropic character of the XXX Hamiltonian that may make its entangling potential
\cite{arnesen2001natural, amico2008entanglement} less sensitive to initial state, measurement settings, etc..
% , is consistent with the fact that the Heisenberg Hamiltonian maximizes the entanglement generation.
Also, it facilitates the implementation in the experimental platforms, where large anisotropic couplings are feasible, but nonetheless more challenging to achieve than isotropic ones \cite{kim2024realization}. 


