    \item negative and increasing on $I_3=[t_1, t_2),$
    \item positive and increasing on $I_4=[t_2, \infty)$. 
\end{enumerate}
Some of these intervals may be empty, for example, if $f(t)\geq 0$, then $I_2=I_3=\varnothing$. Now for the self-adjoint element $x\in \M$ we set $p_i=e_{I_i}(\Phi(x))$ and let $E(y)=\sum_{i=1}^4 p_i y p_i$. 
