0 & p_2 f(\Phi(x)) p_2 & 0 & 0\\
0 & 0 & p_3 f(\Phi(x)) p_3 & 0\\
0 & 0 & 0 & p_4 f(\Phi(x)) p_4
\end{bmatrix}.\]
Note that for $i=1, 4$, $p_i f(\Phi(x)) p_i\geq 0$ and for $i=2, 3$, we have $p_i f(\Phi(x)) p_i\leq 0$.

However, $\Phi(f(x))$ is not diagonal, and we have 

\[E(\Phi(f(x)))=\begin{bmatrix}
