\section{Conclusion}
For interfered saturated echoes in SAR, non-linear saturation leads to the generation of various new interference components. Existing SAR interference suppression methods have a certain degree of model mismatch, and currently there is no model that can accurately describe the SAR saturated echoes impacted by interference. Therefore, this paper proposes an accurate saturated output model based on the Bessel function. Through comparative simulations with the saturation model based on the tanh function, the accuracy of the proposed model is verified, which provides certain guidance for subsequent further analysis of the characteristics of saturated interference signals and interference suppression.



