\section*{Appendix}
\subsection*{A. mLDDMM estimation time}
All the mLDDMM computations were performed on a work station with an Intel i7-1370P with 32 GB RAM and an NVIDIA GeForce MX550. The estimation between the reference and the deformed configuration took about 1h. While the computation time is considerably higher than the computation time for \textit{regular} LDDMM, the framework can be further optimized to reduce the estimation time. Additionally, while  the high detail of the synthetic data served as a complex benchmark to showcase the robustness of the method in tensor extraction, the dimensionality of the discretization significantly influenced the computational time required for the estimation. Further work on diverse, less refined benchmarks should be conducted to evaluate the influence of the mesh complexity on computation time.
