By  Lemma \ref{yl1},  we obtain  that there exists a time $T_{1}^*$ such that for any  $ T< T_1^*,$\\
 $(t,x)\in [0,T]\times \mR^{d},$
\begin{align*}
|\partial^{l}_{2}u^{n}(t,x,\mu^{Z})-\partial^{l}_{2}u^{n}(t,x,\mu^{Z'})|&\leq \bigg|\bigg. \int^{1}_{0}\mE[\partial_{3}\partial_{2}^{l}u^{n}(t,x,\mu^{((1-\theta)Z+\theta Z'
)})(Z-Z')]\dif \theta     \bigg|\bigg.\\
