The following lemma will be  used in subsequent analysis.
\bl\label{ccc5}
Assume the assumption $(\mathrm{H2})$ holds. Then,  for any $\mu^{\epsilon_1}, \mu^{\epsilon_2},$ there exists a constant $C> 0$ such that the solution $u^{\lambda, \mu}$ of Eq.\eqref{37b} satisfies


