\end{align}
where $e_{i}=(0,\cdots, 0, 1, 0,\cdots,0)$
is the standard basis vector with $1$ in the
$i$th position and $0$ elsewhere.
Furthermore, one can see that
\begin{align*}
\nabla^{2}(\theta^{-1}_{it}(\theta_{t}(x)))=(\nabla \theta_{t}(x))^{*} \nabla^{2}\theta^{-1}_{it}(\theta_{t}(x))(\nabla \theta_{t}(x))+ \sum^{d}_{j=1} [\nabla^{2}\theta_{jt}](x)[(\nabla \theta^{-1}_{it})(\theta_{t}(x))]_{j}.
