\section{Predicting variant effects from genomic features}\label{sec: architecture}

Now we have a method for accurately and efficiently training a large model $f_\theta$.
Here we specify how we build $f_\theta$ that include many more functional and comparative genomics features than previous works in Sec.~\ref{sec: f theta features}.
We describe large flexible neural network architectures for $f_\theta$ in Sec.~\ref{sec: f theta architecture}.
The result is a flexible function that predicts the effect of a variant from a variety of genomic information (Fig.~\ref{fig:preds}).

