\section{Photoelectrons emission and micro-LEDs}
\subsection{Experimental setup}

Experiment was set up to demonstrate photoelectric effect generated by micro-LEDs(see Figure \ref{sch&pho}). The dimensions and electrodes distribution of the experimental setup for charge management system were designed with reference to LISA and LISA Pathfinder. This replaces our parallel plate experimental setup performed previously. A test mass(TM) was a cube with 46 mm in length and there was a gap of 5 mm between the test mass and the
electrodes mounted on the electrode housing. Both the surface of the test mass and the inner surface of the electrode housing were gold-coated with a thickness of 500 nm. The test mass was fixed inside the electrode housing by insulated Ultem-1000 holding tubes. Micro-LEDs were installed at the top corners of the housing and directly illuminate the test mass. A contact probe was mounted on the centre of the upper surface of the test mass to read out the potential of the test mass. Bias electrodes were grounded or connected to an external voltage source to provide the bias voltage.

