Several versions of ReservoirChat were created with varying content and database sizes (Figure \ref{fig-comparison-training-doc}). The Basic version includes resolved issues related to ReservoirPy, its complete documentation and code, along with code samples, resulting in a corpus of 70 documents. The Little version includes 10 additional research papers about Reservoir Computing. Medium has 10 more research documents appended to its database, including a PhD thesis. Finally, Big includes all previous resources with 10 additional scientific papers, and a compilation of 245 prepared questions and answers, including 55 code-related questions, and 195 about various concepts related to Reservoir Computing and ReservoirPy. The Big version is the one currently available on the website.

However, GraphRAG also has its limitations. The construction of the permanent knowledge graph requires the precise extraction of entities and relations from the source documents. This requires additional data preprocessing to guarantee the quality of the graph. It also needs to be regularly updated with new information to stay relevant, which can be computationally expensive.






