]
from sklearn.datasets import load_iris 
iris = load_iris()

x = iris.data[:, :2]  # First two features: sepal length and width
y = iris.target

gcor(x, y, alpha=1)

Output: Categorical Gini Correlation: 0.357026
\end{lstlisting}

In Listing~\ref{lst:gcor2}, both sepal length and width are used as predictor variables. The \texttt{gcor} function computes the CGC between the multivariate predictor \( \bi{X} \) and the species labels \( Y \).

\begin{lstlisting}[language=Python, 
  backgroundcolor=\color{lightgray}, 
  basicstyle=\footnotesize\ttfamily, 
